**Issue**: #266
**Date**: 2026-08-25
**Status**: Approved
**Author**: NMG

@issue-266 @bug @plugin-install
Feature: Materialize only explicitly owned plugin controller paths
  nmg-sdlc must resolve packaged controllers independently of consumer cwd
  without claiming ordinary project-local script commands in runtime text.

  Scenario: Project-local command remains unchanged
    Given runtime text contains "node scripts/check-gate.mjs"
    And the installed plugin does not ship "scripts/check-gate.mjs"
    When controller paths are materialized
    Then the runtime text still contains "node scripts/check-gate.mjs"
    And no controller resolution error is raised

  Scenario: Explicit plugin controller resolves absolutely
    Given runtime text contains "node <plugin-root>/scripts/sdlc-execute.mjs"
    And the installed plugin ships "scripts/sdlc-execute.mjs"
    When controller paths are materialized
    Then the placeholder is replaced by the JSON-quoted absolute controller path
    And the consumer project cwd is not used for resolution

  Scenario: Missing explicit controller fails closed
    Given runtime text contains "node <plugin-root>/scripts/missing.mjs"
    And the installed plugin does not ship "scripts/missing.mjs"
    When controller paths are materialized
    Then materialization fails with reason code "controller_unresolved"
    And no project-local script fallback is used

  Scenario: Extension context accepts project verification evidence
    Given installed extension context contains "node scripts/check-gate.mjs"
    When the extension materializes runtime messages
    Then context processing completes without a controller resolution error
    And the project command remains unchanged

  Scenario: Bootstrap replaces an existing pinned Git plugin
    Given nmg-pi bootstrap plans the remote nmg-sdlc commit installation
    And an nmg-sdlc Git dependency is already installed
    When the install plan is executed by OMP 18
    Then the plugin install command includes "--force"
    And the supported force-reinstall path avoids Bun's unchanged-source dependency loop
